# RamJob milestone steering

## Current milestone

**M5 — ETW discovery, adaptive polling, budget CI**  
Prior: M4 closed on `milestone/m4-job-backstop` (thermo + ticket 46 APPROVED `7c1a0a0`).  
Do not start M6 until M5 thermo Critical/Important = 0.

## Pipeline (every milestone / plan)

Do these in order. Do not skip to coding.

1. **Brainstorm** (`/brainstorming`) before any implementation plan.
   - Lead every option set with a **recommendation first**, then alternatives.
   - One clarifying question at a time.
   - No code until the design is approved and written.
2. **Grill with docs** (`/grill-with-docs`) when product/OPEN decisions are still fuzzy after brainstorm — retain answers in `SPEC.md` (and design docs under `docs/superpowers/specs/`). Use SPEC as the stateful glossary; do not invent a parallel truth file.
3. **Update SPEC** as source of truth whenever a decision lands (resolved OPENs, milestone shape, thresholds). Design docs amend SPEC; they do not replace it.
4. **Docs are not truncated.** SPEC and design docs stay complete. Fold amendments into the owning section. Do not replace a full section with a one-line summary that drops rules, tables, or numbers. If content moves, leave a cross-link and keep the canonical text in one place.
5. **writing-plans** after the user approves the written design.
6. **Develop with Subagent-Driven Development (preferred default).** Do not hand-implement milestone tickets in the parent when SDD fits. Controller dispatches `poteto-agent` implementers + reviewers per task. Use poteto-mode on the parent. Follow `.cursor/skills/ramjob-milestone-sdd/SKILL.md`.
7. **Thermo-nuclear code quality review** once per **milestone** (not per task), then fix Critical/Important, then lesson-capture.
8. **Skill creation** when a repeatable process or domain lesson appears — follow `/writing-great-skills` (leading word, checkable Done when, progressive disclosure, no skill spam). Prefer a test/lint over a skill when the lesson is runtime-enforceable. Link new skills from `ramjob-milestone-sdd/lessons/README.md` or promote to `.cursor/skills/` / this `.mdc` when they are always-on.
9. **Commits:** one git commit per SDD task (or named phase). Message references the ticket. Branch `milestone/mN-…`.

## How to build (implementation phase)

1. **Prefer SDD.** Parent coordinates; does not soak context writing the whole milestone. Exception: one-liner / single-file fix after thermo when spinning an implementer costs more than the edit.
2. Tickets only under `.scratch/ramjob/issues/` for the current milestone.
3. Every code `Task` → `poteto-agent` (thermo subagent is the milestone-end exception).
4. Ledger: `.superpowers/sdd/progress.md`.
5. Never two implementers on the same crate/tree.

## Skill creation (proper use)

Use `/writing-great-skills` + Cursor `create-skill` when encoding agent process:

| Prefer | When |
|---|---|
| Harness assert / clippy / CI | Lesson is enforceable at runtime or build |
| Lesson skill under `ramjob-milestone-sdd/lessons/` | Repeatable agent-process failure mode |
| Project skill under `.cursor/skills/` | Reusable workflow with a clear leading word (user- or model-invoked deliberately) |
| This `.mdc` bullet | Always-on RamJob constraint that must load every session |

Rules: one failure mode → one skill; leading word; checkable completion criteria; no no-op prose; no truncation of SPEC when the skill only points at it.

## Model selection (coding Tasks)

Parent (this chat) plans, brainstorms, reviews, and dispatches. **Coding implementers and fix agents must use a weaker model than the parent.**

| Rule | Binding |
|---|---|
| Strength | Coding `Task` model is strictly weaker / cheaper than the parent model (never equal or stronger). |
| Family match | If the parent is a **Cursor** model (Composer / Cursor-branded), dispatch **Cursor** models only. If the parent is another provider (Claude, GPT, Grok API, etc.), dispatch a weaker model from **that same family**, not a Cursor model (and not a cross-family jump). |
| Who it applies to | Implementer and fix `poteto-agent` Tasks that write code. |
| Who it does not force-weaken | Parent controller; brainstorming; writing-plans; grill-with-docs; milestone thermo (judgment may stay strong). Task reviewers may use mid-tier in-family, still not stronger than parent. |
| Always set `model:` | Do not omit `model` on coding Tasks (omission inherits the parent and violates “weaker”). |

Pick the weakest in-family model that can still follow a precise task brief. Mechanical 1–2 file tasks → fastest tier. Multi-file integration → mid tier, still below parent.

## M1 lessons (non-negotiable)

- Runtime yield → **Ry_live**, not Ry_bench.
- Trim measurement → **lock across settle**.
- No premature process-global caches (caller-owned).
- NtQSI/trim errors → `Result` / diagnostics, never `.expect` in the hot path.
- Use `scripts/dev-env.ps1` when `link.exe` / SDK libs are missing.

## On failure

When an approach fails or a review/thermo finding costs a redo:

1. Classify one-off vs repeatable.
2. Prefer a test/assert if enforceable.
3. Else add/update a lesson under `.cursor/skills/ramjob-milestone-sdd/lessons/` and link from `lessons/README.md`.
4. **Update this `.mdc`** under “Failure log” (date + what changed).
5. If the failure changes product truth, **update SPEC** in full (no truncated patch).

